&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change the way the world travels&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the GetYourGuide journey to connect people with unforgettable travel experiences around the world. Millions look to us for unique activities they can trust, and it’s all powered by our commitment to make every single journey extraordinary - including yours.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to unlock your potential with a community of fellow explorers? Find your next role at our Berlin HQ or one of our local offices around the globe, from New York to Bangkok. Head to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.getyourguide.careers/&quot;&gt;getyourguide.careers&lt;/a&gt; to take the first step.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a driven, resilient, and results-oriented &lt;strong&gt;New Business Development Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to strengthen our expert Sales Team in &lt;strong&gt;Tokyo&lt;/strong&gt;. In this role, you will play a pivotal part in our growth by acquiring the best and most popular things to do in travel destinations. You will focus on building and managing a high-performing sales pipeline, negotiating optimal terms, and driving supplier acquisition in &lt;strong&gt;Japan.&lt;/strong&gt; This is a unique opportunity to directly impact millions of travelers while advancing GetYourGuide’s position in the experience industry..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Identify, Acquire and onboard new suppliers&lt;/strong&gt;, primarily tour and experience providers, as well as attractions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively manage the entire sales funnel, including &lt;strong&gt;outreach, negotiation, closing&lt;/strong&gt;, and onboarding, to consistently hit and exceed quota.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate&lt;/strong&gt; with internal teams to align supplier acquisition with broader business goals, ensuring sustainable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent GetYourGuide at relevant industry events to drive acquisition and establish credibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly travel (up to 25%) to build strong relationships with suppliers in destination and create long-term partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your toolkit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 3+ years of experience in B2B sales, with a proven track record of exceeding sales targets, running a disciplined, data-driven process, and confidently using sales tools and software — including CRM (e.g., Salesforce) and sales enablement tools.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are resilient, hungry for success, and thrive under pressure, consistently raising the bar for yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You speak &lt;strong&gt;Japanese at a native level&lt;/strong&gt; as well as proficiency in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You excel at handling objections, reframing conversations with insights, and creating constructive tension to close challenging deals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You bring strong problem-solving skills, using data to prioritize actions and inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an excellent communicator, able to articulate value propositions clearly to diverse audiences, adapting your approach for maximum impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You collaborate with peers, share best practices, and lift the team to new heights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We want your journey with us to be extraordinary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual personal growth budget and mentorship programs for continuous learning and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from anywhere in the world for 30 days per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid working approach with three days of in office collaboration (Mon, Tue, Thur) and two days of optional at home focus time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to collaborate and socialize with team members through quarterly team events and yearly company-wide events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly transportation and fitness budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discounts for you, your friends, and family on GetYourGuide activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language reimbursement program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health and wellness benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And more…&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Submit your CV/resume in English using the form below. For tips and insights into our hiring process and culture, check out ‘&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.getyourguide.careers/how-we-hire&quot;&gt;how we hire&lt;/a&gt;’ and ‘&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.getyourguide.careers/life-at-getyourguide&quot;&gt;life at GetYourGuide&lt;/a&gt;’. If you have any further questions, please don’t hesitate to get in touch at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:jobs@getyourguide.com&quot;&gt;jobs@getyourguide.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re an equal opportunities employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment is that every qualified person will be evaluated according to their skills regardless of age, gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability status, or religion. Please refrain from including your picture and age with your application.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change the way the world travels&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the GetYourGuide journey to connect people with unforgettable travel experiences around the world. Millions look to us for unique activities they can trust, and it’s all powered by our commitment to make every single journey extraordinary - including yours.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to unlock your potential with a community of fellow explorers? Find your next role at our Berlin HQ or one of our local offices around the globe, from New York to Bangkok. Head to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.getyourguide.careers/&quot;&gt;getyourguide.careers&lt;/a&gt; to take the first step.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supply Marketing turns suppliers into long-term partners by owning the B2B marketing funnel from first touch to loyalty — exciting, engaging, and enabling them to grow with us.&amp;nbsp;For example, we run joint campaigns with top suppliers and promote them across a mix of internal and external marketing channels. By providing exposure and helping suppliers with their business needs, these campaigns are a powerful way for GetYourGuide to strengthen strategic relationships and can be leveraged to negotiate better commercial terms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Partnerships Lead, NEA&lt;/strong&gt; with a strong emphasis on &lt;strong&gt;Japan&lt;/strong&gt; (and surrounding markets such as China, South Korea, and Taiwan depending on scope). This role sits at the intersection of &lt;strong&gt;B2B partner marketing, strategic supplier growth, and cross-functional execution&lt;/strong&gt;, with a focus on building high-impact programs for priority suppliers and navigating the unique needs of the Japanese market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A core part of the role is owning the &lt;strong&gt;destination / DMO partnership motion in Japan&lt;/strong&gt;: securing external sponsorship funding and translating destination partnerships into measurable growth (GMV uplift and accelerated supply onboarding), leveraging tourism boards and public-sector stakeholders as strategic multipliers for GetYourGuide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior individual contributor role with high ownership, visibility, and partner-facing responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the NEA supply marketing strategy with a strong focus on Japan — adapting global supply marketing strategy to local market dynamics, partner needs, and growth priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strategic relationships with top attractions, tour operators, and key ecosystem stakeholders — including government agencies / destination bodies / tourism boards where relevant.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage a destination/DMO partnership pipeline to secure external sponsorship support that subsidizes customer acquisition and drives GMV volume for GetYourGuide.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, pitch, negotiate, and execute joint marketing initiatives (e.g., co-marketing campaigns, seasonal demand pushes, product launches, always-on visibility packages), ensuring win-win outcomes for GetYourGuide and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Sales / Supply leadership to support supplier acquisition and development efforts — using marketing and destination partnerships as levers to unlock strategic relationships, improved commercial terms, and faster onboarding pathways.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert destination partner relationships into scalable supply acceleration (e.g., one-to-many onboarding initiatives, warm introductions, whitelists, and partner-enabled lead generation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end program execution by working cross-functionally with campaign managers and internal marketing teams to deliver initiatives on time and to a high quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop high-impact narratives and presentations — translating partner goals into compelling proposals supported by clear value propositions and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track performance and iterate: define success metrics, report on results, and continuously improve programs based on insights and partner feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your toolkit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in B2B marketing, partnerships, business development, sales, supplier/account management, or strategic programs (agency experience considered if you’ve led complex partner programs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fluent in Japanese and English&lt;/strong&gt;. You can confidently present, negotiate, and build trust in Japanese business settings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Critical: hands-on experience working with Japanese businesses in Japan&lt;/strong&gt; (not only with overseas branches). You understand local business norms, relationship-building, decision-making processes, and the nuances/unspoken rules—especially in public-sector contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building and scaling partner marketing programs (co-marketing, joint business plans, go-to-market initiatives, partner enablement, etc.).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly preferred: experience working with government agencies, tourism boards, municipalities, public-sector bodies, or similar — ideally involving procurement processes, formal partnerships, tenders, or multi-stakeholder governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially sharp and outcome-driven: comfortable building a pipeline, negotiating funding/value exchange with senior stakeholders, and translating partnerships into measurable growth outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management: you can align Sales, Marketing, Product, and Ops around shared outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic (think 6+ months ahead) but hands-on and execution-oriented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, negotiation, and storytelling skills; comfortable influencing without authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical and impact-driven: you care about measurable outcomes and can translate insights into action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the Japan travel / attractions / tours landscape is a strong advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Extras that give you an edge&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in digital marketing (paid, CRM, onsite merchandising, performance measurement) and/or brand marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise-level attractions (museums, observation decks, theme parks), transportation-linked experiences, or large tour operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across multiple NEA markets beyond Japan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How we’ll make your career journey extraordinary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Annual personal growth budget and mentorship programs for continuous learning and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from anywhere in the world for 30 days per year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid working approach with three days of in office collaboration (Mon, Tue, Thur) and two days of optional at home focus time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities to collaborate and socialize with team members through quarterly team events and yearly company-wide events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monthly transportation and fitness budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discounts for you, your friends, and family on GetYourGuide activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language reimbursement program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Health and wellness benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And more…&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How to apply&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Submit your CV/resume in English using the form below. For tips and insights into our hiring process and culture, check out ‘&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.getyourguide.careers/how-we-hire&quot;&gt;how we hire&lt;/a&gt;’ and ‘&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.getyourguide.careers/life-at-getyourguide&quot;&gt;life at GetYourGuide&lt;/a&gt;’. If you have any further questions, please don’t hesitate to get in touch at &lt;a href=&quot;mailto:jobs@getyourguide.com&quot;&gt;jobs@getyourguide.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re an equal opportunities employer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment is that every qualified person will be evaluated according to their skills regardless of age, gender identity, ethnicity, sexual orientation, disability status, or religion. Please refrain from including your picture and age with your application.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;世界の旅のあり方を変えよう&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GetYourGuideの一員として、世界中の人々を忘れられない旅行体験へとつなぐ旅に参加しませんか。何百万人ものユーザーが、信頼できるユニークなアクティビティを求めて私たちを利用しています。それを支えているのは、すべての旅を特別なものにするという私たちのコミットメントです――それはあなた自身の旅も含まれます。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;探究心あふれる仲間たちとともに、自分の可能性を広げる準備はできていますか？ベルリン本社、またはニューヨークからバンコクまで世界各地の拠点で、あなたにぴったりのポジションを見つけてください。最初の一歩は getyourguide.careers から。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;チームのミッション&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;サプライマーケティングは、サプライヤーを長期的なパートナーへと変えることを目的とし、最初の接点からロイヤルティに至るまでのB2Bマーケティングファネル全体を担います。魅力的で、エンゲージメントを高め、サプライヤーが当社とともに成長できるよう支援します。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;例えば、主要サプライヤーとの共同キャンペーンを実施し、社内外の多様なマーケティングチャネルを通じてプロモーションを行っています。サプライヤーに露出機会を提供し、ビジネスニーズを支援することで、これらのキャンペーンは戦略的関係を強化し、より良い商業条件の交渉にもつながる重要な手段となります。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;現在、日本を含む北東アジア地域のパートナーシップリードを募集しています。特に日本市場（および必要に応じて中国、韓国、台湾など周辺市場）に重点を置いたポジションです。本ポジションは、B2Bパートナーマーケティング、戦略的サプライヤー獲得、部門横断的な実行の交差点に位置し、戦略的なパートナー向けのプログラム構築と、日本市場特有のニーズへの対応に注力します。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;本ポジションの重要な役割の一つは、日本におけるDMO（観光局）パートナーシップの推進です。外部スポンサー資金の確保や、観光局・公共機関との連携を通じて、GMV（流通総額）の向上や掲載商品の拡充といった測定可能な成長へとつなげます。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;本ポジションは、高いオーナーシップと重要度が高い、パートナー対応を担うシニアレベルポジションです。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ミッション（職務内容）&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本を中心とした北東アジア地域のサプライマーケティング戦略を策定・推進し、グローバル戦略を現地市場に適応させる&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;主要な観光施設、ツアーオペレーター、政府機関・観光局などのステークホルダーとの戦略的関係を構築・維持する&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;外部スポンサー資金を獲得するためのDMOパートナーシップのパイプラインを構築・管理する&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;共同マーケティング施策（キャンペーン、季節プロモーション、新商品ローンチなど）の企画・提案・交渉・実行を行う&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;営業・サプライ部門と連携し、マーケティングを通じてサプライヤー獲得・育成を支援する&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;パートナー関係を活用し、掲載商品拡大を推進する（例：一括登録施策など）&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;社内のマーケティングチームと連携し、プログラムの企画から実行までをリードする&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;高い説得力を持つ提案資料・ストーリーを作成する&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;KPIを設定し、成果を測定・分析しながら継続的に改善する&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;応募要件（スキル・経験）&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B2Bマーケティング、パートナーシップ、事業開発、営業、アカウント管理などで7年以上の経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本語・英語ともにビジネスレベルで流暢&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本国内企業との実務経験（海外拠点のみは不可）&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本特有の商習慣や意思決定プロセスへの深い理解（特に公共分野）&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;パートナーマーケティングプログラムの構築・拡大経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;官公庁や観光局などとの協業経験があれば尚可&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;高いビジネス感覚と成果志向&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;優れたステークホルダーマネジメント能力&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;戦略的思考と実行力の両立&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;優れたコミュニケーション・交渉・ストーリーテリング能力&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;データ分析に基づいた意思決定能力&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本の旅行・観光業界への理解があれば尚可&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;歓迎スキル&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;デジタルマーケティングまたはブランドマーケティングの経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;大規模観光施設やツアー会社との業務経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;日本以外の北東アジア市場での業務経験&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;福利厚生&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;年間の自己成長予算およびメンタープログラム&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;年間30日間のリモートワーク（海外可）&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;週3日のオフィス勤務＋2日の在宅勤務のハイブリッド体制&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;チームイベント・全社イベント&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;交通費・フィットネス補助&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;GetYourGuideのアクティビティ割引&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;語学学習補助&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;健康・ウェルネス支援&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ほか多数&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;応募方法&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;英語の履歴書を提出してください。採用プロセスや企業文化については「how we hire」「life at GetYourGuide」をご覧ください。ご質問は jobs@getyourguide.com までお気軽にお問い合わせください。&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;多様性と機会均等について&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;当社は機会均等を重視しています。年齢、性自認、人種、性的指向、障がい、宗教に関わらず、すべての応募者をスキルに基づいて公平に評価します。履歴書には写真や年齢の記載は不要です。&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change the way the world travels&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the GetYourGuide journey to connect people with unforgettable travel experiences around the world. Millions look to us for unique activities they can trust, and it’s all powered by our commitment to make every single journey extraordinary - including yours.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to unlock your potential with a community of fellow explorers? Find your next role at our Berlin HQ or one of our local offices around the globe, from New York to Bangkok. Head to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.getyourguide.careers/&quot;&gt;getyourguide.careers&lt;/a&gt; to take the first step.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Business Operations &amp;amp; Strategy team at GetYourGuide is the engine behind our commercial growth — turning strategic ambition into operational reality. We work across the full supplier acquisition lifecycle, combining data-driven insight, process excellence, and cross-functional collaboration to ensure GetYourGuide offers the world’s most compelling inventory of travel experiences. From scaling our fastest-growing acquisition channels to optimising vendor partnerships, we move fast, think big, and hold ourselves accountable to measurable impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Business Operations &amp;amp; Strategy, the Inside Sales mission team is responsible for the strategy and economics of our outsourced Inside Sales channel — our highest-velocity route to acquiring new suppliers and activities. As &lt;strong&gt;Revenue Operations Manager for Inside Sales&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the strategic direction, financial performance, and scalability of this channel: building the forecasting and unit-economics framework that governs it, designing the systems and processes that drive its growth, and ensuring our vendor partnership operates as one well-governed lever within a much larger machine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will define the strategy and economics behind GetYourGuide&#39;s fastest-growing supplier acquisition channel — building the models, forecasts, and processes that let us scale it predictably and profitably. You will work closely with Commercial, Data, and Finance to turn channel performance into clear strategic decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the channel&#39;s financial and operating model — building forecasts, tracking unit economics (cost per acquisition, ROI, lifetime value), and using them to guide investment and resourcing decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and act on opportunities to improve channel efficiency through data analysis, tooling, and automation — including the application of AI tools where relevant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex operational and commercial questions into clear, actionable plans, and communicate progress and priorities to senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the channel&#39;s targets and KPIs, and build the analytical frameworks (funnel conversion, cohort performance, benchmarking) needed to track and improve them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the analytical backbone connecting Commercial, Data, and Product — translating channel performance into clear recommendations and trade-offs for senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
