&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The FP&amp;amp;A team’s mission is to be a trusted business partner with a seat at the table to enable the business to make the right decisions through financial insight in a timely manner to achieve our company objectives. We lead the planning process, shape the strategy, and provide management guidance on all key financial decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in the Berlin headquarters and reporting to the Head of Marketing FP&amp;amp;A you will work closely with the Marketing, Finance, and Analytics teams to drive timely and effective decision making. You will be analytically minded with a focus on results providing leadership with clear, concise recommendations that are critical to the company and its success!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structure ambiguous problems.&lt;/strong&gt; Break open questions into testable parts, form a hypothesis, pull the data to prove or disprove it, and land on a recommendation. Work backwards from the decision leadership needs to make.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactively surface insights&lt;/strong&gt; and recommendations that steer marketing investment decisions and accelerate growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the analysis end to end.&lt;/strong&gt; Define, build, and maintain the financial and operational reporting for your marketing channels, then dive deep to find the drivers behind every material variance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build investment business cases.&lt;/strong&gt; Size the opportunity, define the trade-off criteria, and quantify the return so marketing leads and finance can decide with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribute to strategy.&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare the analysis behind trading reviews, QBRs, and planning cycles, and take ownership of specific strategic questions across the marketing portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Simplify for leadership.&lt;/strong&gt; Turn complex analysis into concise, written recommendations that a non-finance reader can follow and act on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your toolkit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of relevant experience in FP&amp;amp;A, business analytics, strategy, or another data-heavy commercial role within a fast-paced and dynamic business environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL: you can independently write and debug non-trivial queries against a data warehouse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data warehouse structure sufficient to sanity-check your own numbers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated habit of turning ambiguous questions into a hypothesis, a query, and a recommendation, not just a report&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using BI tools (e.g. Tableau) to build dashboards and reporting, not just consume them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI first mindset, a key driver in delivering on change and leveraging tools to accelerate performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytically minded, using data coupled with sound business judgement to influence business decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and experience distilling and presenting complex analyses into recommendations to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectual curiosity, passion for problem-solving, and comfort with ambiguity offering a strategic perspective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High energy and a desire to work in a results-oriented, fast-paced environment with the ability to take the initiative and drive work&lt;/li&gt;
